Input/focus requirements

During the splash:

* the first-run dialog must not exist as an active navigation scope;
* no language button should be focusable;
* splash remains non-navigable as it currently is.

Once the first-run dialog appears:

* its existing navigation scope becomes active;
* the browser-preferred supported language may receive initial focus as it does now;
* Enter/gamepad A/click/tap must choose normally;
* Back remains intentionally ineffective.

Once the language is chosen:

* remove the dialog’s navigation scope exactly once;
* hide the dialog;
* prevent stale focus from remaining on a removed/hidden language button;
* enter Home normally.

Avoid race conditions or duplicate Home navigation.

Race/cancellation safety

Preserve the splash screen’s existing run/active() protections.

The post-splash continuation should happen exactly once per completed splash run.

A stale splash run that has been exited or superseded must not later open the language dialog or send the application Home.

Do not add arbitrary timers for sequencing. Use the completion of the existing splash lifecycle.

